1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,225
LEGO bricks come in a fixed set of shapes and colours. That is exactly why everything fits together. A design system is a LEGO set for a product.

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:22,145
Tokens are the named values at its heart: colours, spacing and corners. Name them by role, like colour danger, not by look, like red.

3
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:33,075
A design system also has ready-made components: buttons, inputs, cards and alerts, each with its states and rules.

4
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:39,595
Big examples include Google's Material Design and Apple's guidelines.

5
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:46,800
Solve accessibility once, inside the component, and every screen gets it for free.

6
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:54,075
Because components use roles, dark mode just swaps the token values.

7
00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:02,555
Change the brand colour in one place, and the whole product follows. Now refactor the page with tokens.

